     "content": "### **Yes, you should accept this offer.** \n\nSecuring a **$200,000 sign-on bonus** and matching your base salary to **$240,000** completely shifts the risk/reward calculus in your favor. You successfully extracted near top-of-market value for a Google L6 PM.\n\n---\n\n### 1. Breakdown of the Numbers\n\nGoogle typically vests new-hire RSUs on a front-loaded schedule (usually **33% / 33% / 22% / 12%** or **38% / 32% / 20% / 10%**) rather than a flat 25%/year. \n\nAssuming the standard 33/33/22/12 structure:\n\n| Component | Current (Meta IC6) | Google Year 1 | Google Year 2 (est.) |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Base Salary** | $240,000 | $240,000 | $240,000 |\n| **Target Bonus** | ~$36,000 (15%) | $48,000 (20%) | $48,000 |\n| **Sign-on Bonus** | $0 | **$200,000** | $0 |\n| **Equity Vesting** | ~$250,000 | **$356,400** (33%) | $356,400 + Y1 Refreshes |\n| **Total Comp (TC)** | **~$526,000** | **~$844,400** | **~$644,000 \u2013 $700,000** |\n\n*(Even if Google uses a flat 25%/yr equity schedule, Year 1 Total Comp is **~$758,000**).*\n\n---\n\n### 2. Why This is a Big Win\n\n1. **Guaranteed Cash Replaces Variable Equity:** You aren't just offsetting the $200k in Meta RSUs; you are getting it in **liquid cash** upfront instead of waiting for Meta stock to vest over 12 months.\n2. **Massive Year 1 Jump:** Your Year 1 compensation jumps by **44% to 60%** over your current Meta package.\n3. **No Drop in Years 2\u20133:** Because Google front-loads the first two years of equity, your Year 2 compensation will comfortably remain in the **$650,000\u2013$700,000 range**, providing plenty of runway before any potential equity drop-off in Year 4.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Checklists / Final Questions Before You Sign\n\nBefore clicking \"Accept,\" review the formal offer letter to verify these terms:\n\n* **Sign-on Payout & Clawback:** Confirm if the $200,000 is paid as a lump sum in your first paycheck or split across Year 1 / Year 2. Note the clawback terms (typically a 1- or 2-year prorated repayment if you leave voluntarily).\n* **Vesting Cadence:** Confirm whether the equity vests monthly or quarterly, and verify the exact annual split (e.g., 33/33/22/12).\n* **Start Date Timing:** Ensure your start date allows you to capture any imminent bonus or quarterly RSU vest at Meta if it is within a few weeks.\n\n### Conclusion\nThis is a high-upside, well-negotiated offer. Once you verify the sign-on payment terms, **sign the offer and congratulate yourself on a successful negotiation.**",
